  "limitations": [
    {
      "description": "the corpus walk consults neither the analyzer's carrier table nor the differential oracle's, which is the point: a differential cannot contradict a premise it shares. What it CANNOT do is rule on whether a pair should be a carrier — that judgement is a human decision, so an unreviewed pair fails here and must be ruled in RULED_NOT_A_CARRIER or added as a rule"
    },
    {
      "description": "looksLikeReference is deliberately generous and errs toward asking, because a false candidate costs one line of ruling while a missed carrier is an absent dependency nobody reports. The 61 pairs include presentation, framework-binding and data-* attributes ruled as non-carriers"
    },
    {
      "description": "the corpus is the pinned fixtures repositories and rotates as a pool; the census reports what those files contain, not what the HTML specification permits, so a carrier that no corpus exercises is outside its reach and is covered only by CARRIER_PROBES"
    }
